# D26 axis: auto-infer discipline (NEG) — an explicit `throws MyError`
# declaration WINS over auto-infer. The user declared `throws MyError`;
# even though the body contains a `+!` (which would auto-infer
# ArithError), the rewrite pass leaves the throws-spec alone. The
# resulting `+!` (which produces `Result[int, ArithError]`) then fails
# to auto-propagate into a `MyError`-throws fn — proving the user's
# declaration was preserved (the auto-infer would have made it silently
# work, which is exactly what the discipline rejects).
# Expected diagnostic: `E_UnconvertibleErrorPropagation` naming BOTH
# `ArithError` (the fallible-op's error) and `MyError` (the user's
# explicit throws-spec).
enum MyError:
    Bad()

int add_or_throw(int a, int b) throws MyError:
    return a +! b

void main():
    int r = add_or_throw(2, 3)! catch (e): -1
    print(r)
